# Frontend — Structure Map (`apps/frontend/src`)

## What / Why / How per folder

### Entry
- `index.html` → `main.tsx` mounts `<App />` and loads `index.css`.
- `App.tsx` wraps routes in `AuthProvider`; `PrivateRoute` / `PublicRoute` gate pages by JWT presence.

### `pages/`
- **What**: Route screens split by role — `LoginPage`, `RegisterPage`, `AdminHomePage`, `UsersPage`, `ProjectsPage`, `AdminProjectPage`, `LeadProjectPage`, `MyTasksPage`, `TaskDetailPage`, `TagsPage`.
- **Why**: Admin, project lead, and member each follow a different job after login.
- **How**: Import functions from `api/index.ts`; never raw `fetch` with duplicated auth headers.

### `components/`
- **What**: Shared UI — `Layout` (role nav, notifications), `Sheet`, `AssignmentUI` (assignees, progress, rating).
- **Why**: Reuse across pages without bloating routes.
- **How**: `ProjectDetailPage` renders `AdminProjectPage` or `LeadProjectPage` from `user.role`. Members are sent to My tasks.

### `context/`
- **What**: `AuthContext` — login/register/logout, `isAuthenticated`.
- **Why**: Single auth source for route guards and Layout.
- **How**: Token in `localStorage` via `api/client.ts` (`taskmanager_token`). Login hits `/api/users/login` (form-urlencoded `username`/`password`).

### `api/`
- **What**: `client.ts` (Bearer + error parse), `types.ts` (DTOs), `index.ts` (all endpoints).
- **Why**: One place maps UI → backend paths; Vite proxy makes `/api/...` work in dev.
- **How**: Add new backend endpoints here first, then use from pages. Paths must match `main.py` prefixes.

## Assignment UX path
```
AdminProjectPage
  → setProjectMembers / createTask / setTaskAssignments
  → assignment creates a notification for each new assignee
LeadProjectPage
  → update progress or status → save → project dashboard refreshes → mark completed
MyTasksPage → TaskDetailPage
  → listMyTasks / getTask, read-only for members
```

## Route ↔ page map
| Path | Page | Who |
|------|------|------|
| `/login`, `/register` | Login/Register | Public only. Register always creates a member. |
| `/` | Redirect by role | Private |
| `/admin` | AdminHomePage | Admin |
| `/users` | UsersPage | Admin |
| `/projects` | ProjectsPage | Admin sees all; project lead sees assigned projects |
| `/projects/:projectId` | AdminProjectPage or LeadProjectPage | Admin or the assigned lead |
| `/my-tasks` | MyTasksPage | Any signed-in user |
| `/tasks/:taskId` | TaskDetailPage | Assignee, assigned lead, or admin |
| `/tags` | TagsPage | Admin |

## Frontend → backend connection
```
Page/component
  → api/index.ts (e.g. createTask, generateTaskWithAI)
    → apiRequest("/api/...") + Authorization header
      → Vite proxy (vite.config.ts) → http://localhost:8000
        → FastAPI routers
```

## Coding conventions
- TypeScript types in `api/types.ts` should mirror backend `*Out` schemas.
- After login, rely on `getToken()` automatically attached by `apiRequest`.
- On 401-style failures, prefer logout / redirect to `/login` rather than silent retry loops.
- Keep styling in `index.css` / existing patterns; do not introduce a new CSS framework unless asked.
